{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1579","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Casimir's String Solitaire"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Casimir has a string $$$s$$$ which consists of capital Latin letters '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' only. Each turn he can choose to do one of the two following actions:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" he can either erase exactly one letter '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"and"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" exactly one letter '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' from arbitrary places of the string (these letters don't have to be adjacent); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" or he can erase exactly one letter '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"and"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" exactly one letter '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' from arbitrary places in the string (these letters don't have to be adjacent). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Therefore, each turn the length of the string is decreased exactly by $$$2$$$. All turns are independent so for each turn, Casimir can choose any of two possible actions."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, with $$$s$$$ $$$=$$$ \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ABCABC"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" he can obtain a string $$$s$$$ $$$=$$$ \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ACBC"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" in one turn (by erasing the first occurrence of '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' and the second occurrence of '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'). There are also many other options for a turn aside from this particular example."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For a given string $$$s$$$ determine whether there is a sequence of actions leading to an empty string. In other words, Casimir's goal is to erase all letters from the string. Is there a way to do this?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 1000$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test case is described by one string $$$s$$$, for which you need to determine if it can be fully erased by some sequence of turns. The string $$$s$$$ consists of capital letters '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' and has a length from $$$1$$$ to $$$50$$$ letters, inclusive."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print $$$t$$$ lines, each line containing the answer to the corresponding test case. The answer to a test case should be "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if there is a way to fully erase the corresponding string and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You may print every letter in any case you want (so, for example, the strings "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" will all be recognized as positive answers)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\nABACAB\nABBA\nAC\nABC\nCABCBB\nBCBCBCBCBCBCBCBC\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nNO\nYES\nNO\nNO\nYES\nYES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1579A","schema":2,"sourceK